<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_section">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" title="In 4 Main Results ‣ When Seeing Is not Enough: Revealing the Limits of Active Reasoning in MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Existing MLLMs lack the ability to proactively obtain missing evidence.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" title="In 4 Main Results ‣ When Seeing Is not Enough: Revealing the Limits of Active Reasoning in MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Synthetic images are more challenging.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3" title="In 4 Main Results ‣ When Seeing Is not Enough: Revealing the Limits of Active Reasoning in MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Perception tasks underperform knowledge tasks.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4" title="In 4 Main Results ‣ When Seeing Is not Enough: Revealing the Limits of Active Reasoning in MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Scaling generally improves performance, but not monotonically.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS0.SSS0.Px5" title="In 4 Main Results ‣ When Seeing Is not Enough: Revealing the Limits of Active Reasoning in MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Explicit thinking significantly boosts performance.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section"><a href="#S5" title="In When Seeing Is not Enough: Revealing the Limits of Active Reasoning in MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5 </span>Further Discussions</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_section">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S5.SS1" title="In 5 Further Discussions ‣ When Seeing Is not Enough: Revealing the Limits of Active Reasoning in MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5.1 </span>Active Reasoning is Effective but Limited</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1" title="In 5.1 Active Reasoning is Effective but Limited ‣ 5 Further Discussions ‣ When Seeing Is not Enough: Revealing the Limits of Active Reasoning in MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Active reasoning may exhibit two failure modes.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2" title="In 5.1 Active Reasoning is Effective but Limited ‣ 5 Further Discussions ‣ When Seeing Is not Enough: Revealing the Limits of Active Reasoning in MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Active reasoning can recover missing information.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3" title="In 5.1 Active Reasoning is Effective but Limited ‣ 5 Further Discussions ‣ When Seeing Is not Enough: Revealing the Limits of Active Reasoning in MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">The ability of active reasoning is far from passive reasoning.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S5.SS2" title="In 5 Further Discussions ‣ When Seeing Is not Enough: Revealing the Limits of Active Reasoning in MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5.2 </span>Perception is Crucial for Active Reasoning</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="In 5.2 Perception is Crucial for Active Reasoning ‣ 5 Further Discussions ‣ When Seeing Is not Enough: Revealing the Limits of Active Reasoning in MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Fine-grained difference is more difficult for models to perceive.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="In 5.2 Perception is Crucial for Active Reasoning ‣ 5 Further Discussions ‣ When Seeing Is not Enough: Revealing the Limits of Active Reasoning in MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">More images lead to worse accuracy and longer steps.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS2.SSS0.Px3" title="In 5.2 Perception is Crucial for Active Reasoning ‣ 5 Further Discussions ‣ When Seeing Is not Enough: Revealing the Limits of Active Reasoning in MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Unbalanced between perception and thinking limits the performance.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S5.SS3" title="In 5 Further Discussions ‣ When Seeing Is not Enough: Revealing the Limits of Active Reasoning in MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5.3 </span>Unreliable Verification Limits Gains</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1" title="In 5.3 Unreliable Verification Limits Gains ‣ 5 Further Discussions ‣ When Seeing Is not Enough: Revealing the Limits of Active Reasoning in MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Unreliable verification lengthens the reasoning process</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2" title="In 5.3 Unreliable Verification Limits Gains ‣ 5 Further Discussions ‣ When Seeing Is not Enough: Revealing the Limits of Active Reasoning in MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Benefits of early stopping with single-candidate pools.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S5.SS4" title="In 5 Further Discussions ‣ When Seeing Is not Enough: Revealing the Limits of Active Reasoning in MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5.4 </span>Various Strategies for Improvement</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS4.SSS0.Px1" title="In 5.4 Various Strategies for Improvement ‣ 5 Further Discussions ‣ When Seeing Is not Enough: Revealing the Limits of Active Reasoning in MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Perceptual enhancement yields larger gains than knowledge enhancement.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS4.SSS0.Px2" title="In 5.4 Various Strategies for Improvement ‣ 5 Further Discussions ‣ When Seeing Is not Enough: Revealing the Limits of Active Reasoning in MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Different models require different improvements</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS4.SSS0.Px3" title="In 5.4 Various Strategies for Improvement ‣ 5 Further Discussions ‣ When Seeing Is not Enough: Revealing the Limits of Active Reasoning in MLLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Training thinking modes are better than prompt-based thinking.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
